claimed: acme-revoke -- operator ask 2026-09-07, the one deferred ACME item that is small and testable today: RFC 8555 §7.6 revocation. Acme.revoke(cfg, http, reason) posts the leaf's DER (base64url) to the directory's revokeCert, signed by the ACCOUNT key that ordered it, with an RFC 5280 reason as a named enum (Unspecified, KeyCompromise, Superseded, CessationOfOperation) rather than an integer nobody remembers; a second revoke answers the CA's own alreadyRevoked sentence. An operator needs a way to RUN it, so a small okay.acme.Revoke main beside it, taking the data directory the Serve wiring already uses. Tested against Pebble: the first revoke is accepted, the second refused by name. Touches okay-acme/Acme.scala, a new Revoke.scala, specs/acme.md, docs/modules/okay-acme.md.
